:"2. **Identify the greatest and least members:**\n   - The greatest member is \\(\\frac{11}{8} = 1.375\\).\n   - The least member is \\(\\frac{6}{16} = \\frac{3}{8} = 0.375\\).\n\n3. **Calculate the positive difference between the greatest and the least member:**\n   \\[\n   \\frac{11}{8} - \\frac{3}{8} = \\frac{11 - 3}{8} = \\frac{8}{8} = 1.\n   \\]\n\nThus, the positive difference between the greatest and the least member of the set is \\(\\boxed{1}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{1}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true,"retains_student_answer":false},"graded_text":"To find the positive difference between the greatest and the least member of the set \\(\\left\\{\\frac{3}{7}, \\frac{4}{3}, \\frac{11}{8}, \\frac{6}{16}\\right\\}\\), we first need to determine the decimal or fractional equivalent of each fraction to compare them easily.\n\n1. **Convert each fraction to a decimal or a simpler fraction:**\n   - \\(\\frac{3}{7}\\) is approximately \\(0.428571\\ldots\\).\n   - \\(\\frac{4}{3} = 1.333333\\ldots\\).\n   - \\(\\frac{11}{8} = 1.375\\).\n   - \\(\\frac{6}{16} = \\frac{3}{8} = 0.375\\).\n\n2. **Identify the greatest and least members:**\n   - The greatest member is \\(\\frac{11}{8} = 1.375\\).\n   - The least member is \\(\\frac{6}{16} = \\frac{3}{8} = 0.375\\).\n\n3. **Calculate the positive difference between the greatest and the least member:**\n   \\[\n   \\frac{11}{8} - \\frac{3}{8} = \\frac{11 - 3}{8} = \\frac{8}{8} = 1.\n   \\]\n\nThus, the positive difference between the greatest and the least member of the set is \\(\\boxed{1}\\).","id":"prealgebra:855"}
